This extension adds Nioh 3 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "dinput8.dll".[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "RDBExplorer.exe" to the "package" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "yumia_mod_insert_into_rdb.exe" to the "package" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "LooseFileLoader.dll" to the "plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "Nioh3ModManager.exe" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file with one of these extensions: ".g1t", ".g1m" or ".g1ts".[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file with one of these extensions: ".dll" or ".asi" to the "plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "package" and a file with one of these extensions: ".fdata" or ".yumiamod.json" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above is installed to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

